I have added a second df, containing means of the three subsets
df.mean = ddply(df.1,.(kind),summarise,my.mean=mean(x))

I have extended the plot function to plot a vline
geom_vline(aes(xintercept=my.mean),data=df.mean,linetype="dashed", size=0.5)

It works but plots 2 vlines on the first plot and 3 vlines on the other two.

I read at: http://trinkerrstuff.wordpress.com/2012/09/01/add-text-annotations-to-ggplot2-faceted-plot/:
#### `````````````````````````````````````````````````````
Note that the group=NULL is essential to let ggplot2 know you’re dealing with a new data set and the mapping from before can be forgotten (or at least this is how I understand it).
#### `````````````````````````````````````````````````````

But changing the line as follows, does not help:
geom_vline(aes(xintercept=my.mean,group=NULL),data=df.mean,linetype="dashed", size=0.5)

